_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Removing the depends_on 273a-ae7d-23ac-40c2 blocker: that edge existed only because 273a would create headroom in dispatch_one.py. That headroom already exists (dispatch_one.py is 673/800 LOC after the closed 744a extracted apply phases into dispatch_apply_phases.py). d19d's file_impact is dispatch_one.py (update_one in place), not a dispatch_update.py seam, so 273a is not a prerequisite. 273a marked obsolete (duplicates 744a). See 273a comment for full evidence.","timestamp":1786653651440743001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and pushed to Gerrit as change 1776 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1776).\n\nHeld-out RED oracle tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_outbound_multi_project.py (11 tests) confirmed RED for the right reasons, now GREEN. Mutation-checked: removing the differ stamp, removing the not-synced/foreign-project gate, removing the DC key drop, and reverting the guard set-normalization each returned the relevant tests to RED.\n\nChanges across 5 files: outbound_differ.py (OutboundDiffConfig.projects_mapping + resolve/stamp on the create path under reserved key _bridge_target_project; not-synced/foreign-project emits no create), run_differs.py (load_mapping threaded into the config), acli.py + jira_datacenter/_issues.py (both transports read the reserved key; DC drops it via _BRIDGE_ONLY_CREATE_FIELDS), applier.py (cross-project guard accepts the store's project SET, falls back to single project for unseeded stores).\n\nBlast radius: full tests/unit/rebar_reconciler suite (2716 passed), no-resurrection create-path test (9 passed), existing cross-project guard test green (str-signature compat preserved). make lint + make typecheck clean. All modules under the 800-LOC cap (applier 778). Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before Submit + close.","timestamp":1786720145638393001}],"created_at":1786160100332954001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"454ac14e-7fb1-497e-984e-9b70c92a9d35","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"},{"link_uuid":"8979c2b9-c3ef-4e89-aefc-e406643b6cca","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a40a-364a-8cb2-4923"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nOutbound sync can only write to one tracker project, and it fails closed on anything else. Both\ncreate transports take their project from a single construction-time value — Cloud\n`AcliClient.create_issue` uses `self.jira_project` (`adapters/jira/acli.py:274-330`); DC\n`_IssuesMixin.create_issue` uses `self.project` (`adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:163-189`). And\nthe applier scans every outbound mutation pre-flight and raises `CrossProjectTargetError` — aborting\nthe whole pass — if any update or delete targets a key outside the one configured project\n(`applier.py:230-255`, `_cross_project_targets`, bug `626d`); its sole caller (`applier.py:593-610`)\npasses a single string `select_backend(load_config()).project`. With a mapping listing several\nprojects, correct mutations to the other projects would be treated as the misconfiguration that guard\nexists to catch.\n\n## Approach\n\nThree changes: resolve the create target per ticket (covering BOTH transports), relax the guard to\nset membership, and change the guard's caller to supply the set.\n\n**Create targets the ticket's resolved project — resolved once, above both transports.** The\nresolution happens where the create mutation is BUILT, in `_compute_outbound_create_mutation`\n(`outbound_differ.py:502`), which already receives the full local `ticket` (so it can read\n`bridge_project`). It calls `resolve_project(ticket, mapping)` (`projects_store.py:97-110`) against\nthe store mapping, loaded once via `projects_store.load_mapping(repo_root)` (the `Mapping` that `resolve_project`\nand the `mapping.projects` membership check both require) and threaded into\n`compute_outbound_mutations` as a new optional field on `OutboundDiffConfig`, populated by that\nfunction's sole caller `run_differs.py:466` (which already holds `repo_root`). Three outcomes:\n  * resolves to \"not synced\" (absent→no legacy_default, or explicit `\"\"`) → NO create mutation;\n  * resolves to a key **NOT in `mapping.projects`** → NO create mutation (a stale/typo binding must\n    not create against an unsynced project — this closes the create-side gap the guard cannot, since\n    creates are guard-exempt: their key is a local-id placeholder, so `_JIRA_KEY_RE` never matches);\n  * resolves to a valid in-set key → stamped into the mutation's `fields` under the reserved key\n    `_bridge_target_project`.\n\nBecause the create mutation's `fields` reach whichever `TicketTransport` is active\n(`dispatch_one.create_one` copies `mutation[\"fields\"]` into the `ticket_data` it hands\n`client.create_issue`), resolving here covers Cloud AND Data Center from one site. Each transport\nreads `ticket_data.get(\"_bridge_target_project\")` and falls back to its construction-time value when\nthe key is absent (legacy single-project behaviour preserved): Cloud\n`project = ticket_data.get(\"_bridge_target_project\") or self.jira_project`; DC\n`fields.setdefault(\"project\", {\"key\": ticket_data.get(\"_bridge_target_project\") or self.project})`.\nThe transports handle the reserved key explicitly, because they treat unknown payload keys\nDIFFERENTLY. Cloud's `create_issue` EXTRACTS only the fields it names and ignores the rest, so the key\nnever reaches ACLI. DC's `create_issue` splats the whole TRANSLATED dict into\n`self._client.create_issue(**fields)` — so the key must be DROPPED before the splat or it is sent as a\nbogus Jira field id (the `HTTP 400 … Field … cannot be set` class of bug 18a5). It is added to\n`_BRIDGE_ONLY_CREATE_FIELDS` (`_issues.py:29`) alongside the bridge-only names `title`/`ticket_type`,\nso `_translate_create_fields` reads it for the project then drops it — that drop is what keeps the\nreserved key off the tracker by construction, exactly as the bridge-only names already are.\n\n**The guard relaxes from equality to set membership.** `_cross_project_targets` currently compares\neach target key's prefix against one `configured_project` string; it instead checks membership in the\nmapping's project set. This is the smallest possible weakening: the guard stays fail-closed and still\naborts pre-flight before any tracker write, so a stale binding pointing at a project the store does\nnot sync is caught exactly as today. Only keys the store legitimately owns now pass.\n\n**The guard's caller supplies the set.** The sole caller (`applier.py:593-610`) currently computes a\nsingle `_project = select_backend(load_config()).project`. It instead loads the store's project set\nvia `projects_store.read_projects(repo_root)`, whose keys ARE the project set, and passes that set. An\nempty/absent mapping falls back to the single configured project so single-project stores are\nunchanged.\n\n**Module size.** All touched files stay under the 800-line gate with headroom; each edit is small and\nlocal.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` — resolve + validate + stamp the target\n  project on the create mutation; new optional `OutboundDiffConfig` mapping field\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py` — populate the new config field from the loaded\n  mapping (the sole caller of `compute_outbound_mutations`)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py` — Cloud create reads the payload target\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py` — DC create reads the\n  payload target AND drops the reserved key in `_translate_create_fields`\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py` — guard set-membership + caller supplies the set\n- Read-only dependency: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py` — `load_mapping`/`Mapping`,\n  `resolve_project`, `read_projects` (the authoritative project set)\n- tests under `tests/`\n\n## Testing\n\nTier per the shared standard's external-service row: a stateful fake transport fed production-shaped\nmutations, recording the create calls it receives, because the destination project carried on the\ncall is the contract under test. Both transports are covered.\n\n- Happy path (both transports): a ticket resolving to project `B` in a store whose mapping lists `A`\n  and `B` produces a create call carrying `B`, not the repo default `A` — asserted against the Cloud\n  fake AND the Data Center fake.\n- DC leak guard: the DC fake's recorded create fields do NOT contain `_bridge_target_project`,\n  proving the reserved key is dropped and never sent as a Jira field.\n- Validation edge: a ticket whose `bridge_project` names `Z` (NOT in the `A`/`B` mapping) emits no\n  create mutation — proving a stale/typo binding cannot create against an unsynced project.\n- Contrast case (the guard, both directions in one paired test): an update targeting `B-1` where the\n  mapping lists `A` and `B` proceeds; an update targeting `C-1` still raises `CrossProjectTargetError`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] An outbound create targets the ticket's resolved project rather than the client default on the\n      Cloud transport; checked by a Cloud fake asserting the project on the recorded create call.\n- [x] An outbound create targets the ticket's resolved project on the Data Center transport; checked\n      by a DC fake asserting the project on the recorded create call.\n- [x] The reserved `_bridge_target_project` key is dropped from the DC create field set; checked by\n      asserting it is absent from the DC fake's recorded create fields.\n- [x] A ticket whose resolved project is absent from the mapping set emits no create mutation;\n      checked by asserting an empty mutation list for it.\n- [x] An update inside the configured set proceeds while one outside it raises\n      `CrossProjectTargetError`; checked by a paired test covering both directions.\n- [x] When the guard raises, no tracker write has occurred; checked by asserting the fake recorded\n      zero writes.\n- [x] Single-project behaviour is unchanged; checked by a regression test running the guard against a\n      one-project mapping in both directions.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py","reason":"OutboundDiffConfig.projects_mapping; resolve+stamp target project on the create path under reserved key; not-synced/foreign-project emits no create"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py","reason":"load the store mapping via load_mapping(repo_root) and thread it into OutboundDiffConfig.projects_mapping"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py","reason":"Cloud create_issue reads the reserved _bridge_target_project key for the create project"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py","reason":"DC create reads the reserved key; drop it via _BRIDGE_ONLY_CREATE_FIELDS so it never reaches the tracker"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"cross-project guard accepts the store project SET, falling back to the single configured project for unseeded stores"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_outbound_multi_project.py","reason":"held-out oracle: differ stamp/suppress, Cloud+DC create project + DC key-drop, guard set-membership + str-compat"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","273a-ae7d-23ac-40c2"],["depends_on","cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"],["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"],["relates_to","a40a-364a-8cb2-4923"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"8157521d-777b-47fe-b83f-d6cff9dc5e4e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d19d-7f60-0137-475a","ticket_type":"story","title":"Multi-project outbound dispatch and cross-project guard relaxation to set membership","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["225f32e0-90f8-4d9a-948d-f2bdd2ff0ee3","52c20f05-3a42-47c0-baaa-3865de4d8628","08a96da8-a3d5-4f62-889a-c2fc85c29a8e","7653cd6d-5ca9-411e-bb3e-8683d9c32ab4","dd766f1a-8b36-42f8-9ff1-3d3d7e6f42c0","55a9821f-beb9-4140-b771-13a61f4389ba","611887da-5e13-481f-a5fe-d40b3b67c89d","de753915-94f9-41cb-b560-23b01ef9201d","8979c2b9-c3ef-4e89-aefc-e406643b6cca","03fe2994-0c5c-41a3-bb7c-36d1708975fc","489ab9cb-273a-480e-a07d-e7004b698b57","f9aa4580-cfa2-4ea7-b69a-7e16d6d60e22","8157521d-777b-47fe-b83f-d6cff9dc5e4e","588e0ea2-d0c2-41cb-9ed7-873162f6d58b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786725056000153001,"uuid":"9ac9c21f-9e38-4288-9c30-8b42b52f64e4"}